note tsum: ts(n) = ts(n - 1) + n, ts(0) = 0, on ulong (Omega wraps unsigned values: no check). ts(1000000) is
note 500000500000 (Wolfram), more than 2^31 - 1, so main takes its low byte before `int` (whose check, chk.conv
note trap 5, would otherwise fail): status 32. Under omc the recursion is a million calls deep and traps 6 (exit 106).
fn ts n ulong to ulong
if lt n 1
ret n
end
r = ts sub n 1
ret add r n
end
fn main to int
ret int and ts 1000000 255
end
